```

Potentially we couldn't just explicitly disable the metrics in the default k8s configuration on the kubeletstats receiver side. The problem is that the exclusion on the SignalFx exporter side can potentially be disabled by users. For those users, we actually want to show the warnings.

So we need to temporarily add another converter until the metric is disabled on the kubelet receiver side by default. The converter looks at the SignalFx exporter in the user's config, and if metrics are not explicitly enabled on the exporter side, it disables them on the kubelet receiver side to suppress the warnings.

The conversion required to copy `dpfilters` package from the signal exporter. That copy will be removed along with the converter in a few releases.

